  "articleSummary": "The article argues that LLMs excel at creative reasoning but fail at executing deterministic, sequential business logic—leading to flaky agents. The solution is to use structured workflows for precise, ordered steps (e.g., API calls, validation) and reserve LLMs for creative tasks (e.g., suggestions). A practical weather planner example demonstrates this separation: a deterministic step fetches weather data, then an agent suggests activities. The tone is a tutorial/analysis with pragmatic advice, framing the core metaphor as \"knowing when to tell the model to obey instead of think.\" The audience is developers building production-grade LLM applications, with additional mention of context-window memory issues (truncated in excerpt).",
